Important content rules:
- Do not use generic AI words such as “AI answer”, “prompt”, “chat”, or “ask anything.”
- Use decision-support words: “sort”, “compare”, “fit”, “trade-off”, “backup”, “filtered out.”
- Do not show unrealistic or inappropriate recommendations.
- Because the situation is rainy, low-effort, and 2 hours, avoid hikes, long trips, outdoor-only activities, expensive dinner reservations, or anything far away.
- Make the system show why bad options were removed.
- Make the system show the user’s context on every recommendation screen.

Important visual design rules:
- Keep color palette small and calm.
- Use accent color only for primary actions and selected chips.
- Avoid color pollution.
- Use large clear titles.
- Use readable body text.
- Do not use all-caps except short section labels.
- Use strong visual hierarchy: users should immediately see the main action on each screen.
- Group related elements with cards, spacing, and alignment.
- Put controls next to the items they affect.
- Make all option cards visually consistent.
- Make all context chips visually consistent.
- Follow a consistent grid.
- Keep the logical path clear from top to bottom.
- Make screens feel like one coherent app with screen inertia.